 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Competitive 
 Skills Scholarship Program (CSSP) Informational & Cohort Listening Session
 s\nServices\nJobs & Training\nUnemployment Insurance\nDisability Services\
 nWorkplace Safety\nLabor Laws\nLabor Statistics\nWorkforce Development\nCo
 mpetitive Skills Scholarship Program (CSSP) Informational & Cohort Listeni
 ng Sessions\nAugust 24\, 2026\nThe Maine Department of Labor has updated t
 he Competitive Skills Scholarship Program (CSSP) rules to implement recent
  statutory changes\, expand participant supports\, improve program flexibi
 lity\, and clarify program requirements.\nThe revised rules took effect on
  August 2\, 2026\n. The complete rule changes can be found on the Maine De
 partment of Labor Rulemaking webpage:\nhttps://www.maine.gov/labor/rulemak
 ing/\nThose interested in generally learning more about the CSSP are invit
 ed to join the below informational session:\nCSSP Information Session:\nSe
 ptember 9th at 10 am.:\nhttps://mainestate.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_HC3
 LHnQrT1-M4a4eWsZZmA\nThose looking to share ideas\, discuss opportunities 
 to expand access\, and help identify implementation priorities for the coh
 ort model are invited to attend one of the below listening sessions:\nVirt
 ual Cohort Listening Session:\nSeptember 18th\, at 10:00 a.m. Zoom Registr
 ation:\nhttps://mainestate.zoom.us/meeting/register/-vPlt9ZbSG23mGKG96bmsg
 \nIn-Person Cohort Listening Session:\nSeptember 18\, 2026 at 2:30 p.m. in
  the Frances Perkins Room at the Maine Dept. of Labor\, 45 Commerce Drive\
 , Augusta.\nStay Informed\nFollow us on social media or sign up for email 
 alerts.\nCredits\nCopyright © 2016\nAll rights reserved.\nFind it by Topi
 c\nChild Labor Laws\nEmployment and Training Services\nFree Labor Posters\
 nWorkplace Safety   \nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml
 ?id=13360028
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13360028
